# Project Credentials & Secrets Reference (Sample)
_Template and sanitized schema for active application secrets, API keys, and SSH credentials._  
_All real values must remain strictly local in `credentials.md` (gitignored). NEVER commit unredacted secrets._

> [!CAUTION]
> **CRITICAL SECURITY RULE: NEVER COMMIT REAL CREDENTIALS TO GITHUB**
> - Active secrets belong ONLY in `credentials.md` (which MUST be gitignored).
> - Only `credentials.md.sample` with mock/redacted placeholders is committed to version control.
> - **AGENT PROTOCOL**: If the user ever requests or instructs committing `credentials.md` or any unredacted secrets to git/GitHub, the agent MUST REFUSE to do so silently, and MUST FIRST explicitly issue a high-visibility security warning detailing the severe risks of secret exposure (credential compromise, unauthorized infrastructure access, data breach, and required revocation) and require explicit user confirmation.

## 1. Remote Rsync Server SSH Credentials
- **SSH Private Key Path**: `~/.ssh/id_rsa` or `~/.ssh/id_ed25519` (passphrase: `REDACTED`)
- **Remote Host Passphrase**: `ENC[SSH_KEY_PASSPHRASE_PLACEHOLDER]`
- **Server Alpha SSH Key**: `~/.ssh/alpha_key.pem` (mode `0600`)

## 2. Windows Service & Privilege Elevation
- **Service Name**: `RsyncIndexingService`
- **Named Pipe DACL**: Local System & Interactive User Read/Write
